217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (Matte enlisted in the U.S. Army at 18, but a spinal injury derailed his career and set off years of health and financial hardship. Unable to afford routine care, he avoided treatment until pain became unbearable, resulting in repeated emergency visits and ambulance transports. Over the past decade, he has accumulated more than $300,000 in medical debt. Throughout multiple hospital interactions, charity care was never explained or offered to him. The debt sent his credit score into the low 400s, leading to repeated denials for housing and transportation despite having the means to pay. He is currently facing additional barriers after finding that his Humana insurance is not widely accepted by providers in Austin. If Matte had been screened for charity care, consistent and affordable treatment could have broken the cycle of emergency care, debt, and instability that has defined the last decade of his life.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
