/E (HOW A DAMAGED CREDIT SCORE IMPACTS LIVES)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Jane, a new Austin resident, was rebuilding her life as an electrician apprentice when a stolen car cost her that job and her financial footing. While struggling to recover, she developed cellulitis and returned to the hospital twice for treatment that never resolved it. Despite being covered by insurance, her medical bills were too steep to pay. Instead of receiving an opportunity to get back on her feet, she was faced with repeated threats of collections, and charity care was never offered. Her credit score collapsed, costing her housing, a vehicle, and job opportunities. Jane's story shows how a single treatable illness, mishandled by hospital billing, can quietly destroy a person's credit and their chance at stability.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
